Your Sacred Journey 3 Days 1 to 4
1
Day 1: Delhi ³ Barkot
Your pilgrimage begins with a scenic drive through 
Mussoorie's beautiful hill roads. Arrive in Barkot for overnight 
rest and acclimatization to the mountain climate.
2
Day 2: Yamunotri Darshan
Drive to Janki Chatti, then proceed to Yamunotri Temple via 
trek or pony ride. Take a holy bath in the hot springs and 
receive blessings at the source of River Yamuna. Return to 
Barkot for the night.
3
Day 3: Barkot ³ Uttarkashi
Journey through picturesque Himalayan valleys to Uttarkashi. 
Visit the ancient Kashi Vishwanath Temple and immerse 
yourself in the spiritual atmosphere of this sacred town.
4
Day 4: Gangotri Darshan
Early morning departure for Gangotri, the origin of the holy 
River Ganga. Take a sacred dip, offer prayers at the temple, and 
experience divine tranquility before returning to Uttarkashi.

Divine Darshan 3 Days 5 to 7
Day 5: Uttarkashi ³ 
Guptkashi
Scenic mountain journey through 
winding roads and breathtaking 
vistas. Evening rest allows proper 
acclimatization before the 
Kedarnath helicopter journey.
Day 6: Kedarnath by 
Helicopter
The highlight of your yatra! 
Helicopter transfer from Phata/Sersi 
to Kedarnath Temple. Receive 
blessings at one of the twelve 
Jyotirlingas, situated at 3,583 metres. 
Return to Guptkashi by evening.
Day 7: Guptkashi ³ Badrinath
Drive through Joshimath to Badrinath. Arrive in time for the enchanting evening 
aarti at Badrinath Temple, one of the four sacred Char Dham sites.

Completing Your Pilgrimage 3 
Days 8 to 10
01
Day 8: Badrinath Darshan ³ 
Rudraprayag
Morning darshan at Badrinath Temple 
dedicated to Lord Vishnu. Visit Mana 
Village, the last Indian village before 
Tibet, and witness the mythological Vyas 
Gufa and Ganesh Gufa. Drive to 
Rudraprayag for overnight stay at the 
sacred confluence of Alaknanda and 
Mandakini rivers.
02
Day 9: Rudraprayag ³ Haridwar
Scenic return journey through the 
Himalayan foothills. Arrive in Haridwar 
by evening to witness the mesmerizing 
Ganga Aarti at Har Ki Pauri, a perfect 
spiritual conclusion to your Char Dham 
Yatra.
03
Day 10: Departure
After breakfast, transfer to Haridwar, Rishikesh, or Dehradun for your onward 
journey. Depart with blessed memories and spiritual fulfilment from your sacred 
pilgrimage.

Comfortable Accommodation Throughout
We've carefully selected clean, comfortable hotels at each destination to ensure restful nights after your daily journeys and darshans. All properties 
offer basic modern amenities whilst maintaining proximity to temple sites.
Barkot
